> hda_codec: Unknown model for ALC861, trying auto-probe from BIOS...
> ALSA /home/ionocatabi/down/alsa-hg/alsa-driver/pci/hda/hda_codec.c:2133: autoconfig: line_outs=1 (0xb/0x0/0x0/0x0/0x0)
> ALSA /home/ionocatabi/down/alsa-hg/alsa-driver/pci/hda/hda_codec.c:2137:    speaker_outs=0 (0x0/0x0/0x0/0x0/0x0)
> ALSA /home/ionocatabi/down/alsa-hg/alsa-driver/pci/hda/hda_codec.c:2139:    hp=0x0, dig_out=0x12, din_in=0x0
> ALSA /home/ionocatabi/down/alsa-hg/alsa-driver/pci/hda/hda_codec.c:2147:    inputs: mic=0xd, fmic=0x0, line=0x0, fline=0x0, cd=0x11, aux=0x0
> 
> but still no luck :(
> passing model=asus is of no help, every volume control is up but I can't hear
> sound, nor from line-out nor from internal speakers.  Sound seems to play but I
> can't hear anything.
> 
> any clue on this?

ALC861 has the following model option values:

	  3stack	3-jack
	  3stack-dig	3-jack with SPDIF I/O
	  6stack-dig	6-jack with SPDIF I/O
	  auto		auto-config reading BIOS (default)

Try model=3stack at first.  This was the old default value.


